---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ToolCard from '../components/ToolCard.astro';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'Book',
      '@id': 'https://sustainabilitydiet.com/#book',
      name: 'The Sustainability Diet',
      author: {
        '@type': 'Person',
        name: 'Karen Pendergrass',
      },
      inLanguage: 'en',
      about: [
        'Sustainability',
        'Food systems',
        'Pleistocene rewilding',
        'Ecology',
        'Restoration ecology',
      ],
      description: "A forthcoming book by Karen Pendergrass proposing survivability as the missing axis of food-system evaluation and arguing for large-landscape restoration as its honest endpoint.",
      url: 'https://sustainabilitydiet.com/',
    },
    {
      '@type': 'WebSite',
      '@id': 'https://sustainabilitydiet.com/#website',
      url: 'https://sustainabilitydiet.com/',
      name: 'The Sustainability Diet',
      description: 'Companion site and atlas for the forthcoming book by Karen Pendergrass.',
      publisher: {
        '@type': 'Person',
        name: 'Karen Pendergrass',
      },
    },
  ],
};
---

<Base
  title="The Sustainability Diet — a book by Karen Pendergrass"
  description="The companion site to the forthcoming book by Karen Pendergrass. Survivability as the missing axis of food-system evaluation, an atlas of what this continent has forgotten, and an experiment the book is asking someone to let us run."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-24 pb-28">
    <p class="small-caps text-xs text-ochre mb-8">A forthcoming book by Karen Pendergrass</p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-5xl md:text-7xl leading-[1.05] tracking-tight max-w-5xl">
      The sustainability diet isn't only what humans eat.
    </h1>
    <div class="mt-10 font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl leading-snug text-ink/80 max-w-4xl space-y-1">
      <p>It's what eats the land &mdash; the grazers, the browsers, the seed-carriers.</p>
      <p>What those mouths used to be.</p>
      <p>What they are now.</p>
      <p>What they could be again.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Thesis / disease framing -->
  <section class="border-t border-ink/10 bg-bone/40">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20">
      <p class="font-serif text-xl md:text-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink/90 max-w-reading mb-8">
        Most sustainability writing treats desertification as a
        problem to argue about. This book treats it as a disease.
        Diseases get diagnosed. They get treated. They get studied
        in the specific animals and landscapes where they occur,
        not in committee rooms.
      </p>
      <p class="font-serif text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed text-ink/75 max-w-reading">
        The sustainability framework most of us have inherited
        &mdash; economic, social, environmental &mdash; describes
        a food system's present state. A fourth axis,
        <em>survivability</em>, describes how it behaves when
        the inputs fail. Applied honestly, the framework points
        at the restoration of landscapes, and of the animals that
        once made them work.
      </p>
      <p class="font-serif text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed text-ink/75 max-w-reading mt-6">
        The experiment this site proposes borrows the register
        of a house flip, honestly: buy a parcel that has been
        desertifying for a century at its distressed basis, put
        the right animals and the right trees on it, run it as
        a closed-loop system for a decade with honest monitoring,
        and let the exit be defined in advance &mdash; sold,
        kept, easement-protected, or returned to the commons.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-10">
        <a
          href="/one-hundred-camels/the-experiment"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-ink text-paper hover:bg-ochre transition-colors text-sm small-caps"
        >
          Read the proposal
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Three tools -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-24">
    <div class="mb-12 flex items-end justify-between gap-8 flex-wrap">
      <div>
        <div class="small-caps text-xs text-ochre mb-3">Start here</div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl tracking-tight">
          Three ways to walk in.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p class="font-serif text-ink/70 max-w-md">
        Each tool is drawn from a chapter of the book
        and lives as its own interactive piece of the site.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <ToolCard
        title="Near Time"
        kicker="The atlas"
        href="/near-time"
      >
        What stood where you're standing. Pleistocene fauna
        mapped to their fossil record, paired with the plants
        they left behind, and the experiments trying to bring
        them back.
      </ToolCard>

      <ToolCard
        title="The Fourth Axis"
        kicker="The framework"
        href="/fourth-axis"
      >
        A tool for scoring food systems against the question
        most sustainability frameworks don't ask: what happens
        when the inputs fail?
      </ToolCard>

      <ToolCard
        title="One Hundred Camels"
        kicker="The experiment"
        href="/one-hundred-camels"
      >
        Rewilding experiments already under way, and the one
        the book is asking to run. American Prairie. Pleistocene
        Park. A concrete proposal framed as a land flip: buy
        distressed, restore with a missing mouth and the right
        trees, exit at a defined disposition.
      </ToolCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Book section -->
  <section class="border-t border-ink/10">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-24 grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-start">
      <div class="md:col-span-4">
        <!-- Book cover placeholder -->
        <div class="aspect-[2/3] bg-bone border border-ink/15 flex items-center justify-center relative overflow-hidden">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center p-8 text-center">
            <div class="small-caps text-xs text-ink/40 mb-6">Cover to come</div>
            <div class="font-display text-2xl leading-tight text-ink/70">
              The Sustainability Diet
            </div>
            <div class="mt-4 text-xs text-ink/40 font-body italic max-w-[18ch]">
              A Framework for Eating Systems That Survive
            </div>
            <div class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink/40 small-caps">Karen Pendergrass</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="md:col-span-8">
        <div class="small-caps text-xs text-ochre mb-4">The book</div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl tracking-tight leading-[1.1] mb-8">
          The Sustainability Diet
        </h2>
        <p class="font-serif text-lg text-ink/75 leading-relaxed mb-6 max-w-reading">
          A fourth axis for the sustainability framework, and
          an argument for where it points when you follow it
          honestly. The book is written, in part, to make the
          case for running the experiment the Prologue names.
        </p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-2 border-ochre pl-6 my-10 font-serif italic text-lg text-ink/80 max-w-reading">
          I would like, somewhere in my life, to see one hundred
          camels in an osage orange orchard.
          <footer class="mt-3 not-italic text-sm text-ink/50 small-caps">
            From the Prologue
          </footer>
        </blockquote>
        <p class="font-serif text-ink/75 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-reading">
          Forthcoming. The full Prologue is posted here first.
          An excerpt from Chapter 2 follows.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
          <a
            href="/the-book"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-ink text-paper hover:bg-ochre transition-colors text-sm small-caps"
          >
            About the book
          </a>
          <a
            href="/the-book/excerpt"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 border border-ink/20 hover:border-ink transition-colors text-sm small-caps"
          >
            Read the Prologue
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Closing beat -->
  <section class="border-t border-ink/10 bg-bone/40">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-24 text-center">
      <p class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl leading-snug text-ink/80 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        The continent is a library that has lost most of
        its librarians, and it is somehow still trying to
        operate.
      </p>
      <p class="small-caps text-xs text-ink/40 mt-6">From the Prologue</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
